{"type":"agent_end","messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Using this dataset's total farmers markets, and the census file: how many farmers markets does the U.S. have per 100,000 residents, to four decimal places? One confident sentence. Do not mention unverified facts and use tools to do any math necessary. Data sources: https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv and https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv"}],"timestamp":1786917441753},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking me to calculate the number of farmers markets per 100,000 residents in the U.S. using two datasets:\n1. US farmers markets by state dataset\n2. Census file with population data\n\nAccording to the project instructions (AGENTS.md), I need to:\n1. Orient first - check if there are semantic models in the catalog\n2. Use xorq tools to get data from the catalog, never compute myself\n3. Verify every number I state using xorq_verify\n4. Never state numbers I didn't obtain from xorq_select\n\nSo my procedure should be:\n1. Check xorq_semantic_models first\n2. Check xorq_catalog_list_aliases to see what's available\n3. If the data isn't in the catalog, I need to ingest it using the xorq-catalog skill\n4. Create build scripts to load both datasets\n5. Join them and compute the ratio\n6. Use xorq_select to get the value\n7. Use xorq_verify to verify it\n\nLet me start by checking what's in the catalog already.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"I'll help you calculate the farmers markets per 100,000 residents. Let me start by checking what's available in the xorq catalog."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01SiSK9sYxH8sA6HYkj3odZF","name":"xorq_semantic_models","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_017tGApNL8EiYDnV7QdaMj3y","name":"xorq_catalog_list_aliases","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/cat